+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry owns the boundary between model-produced input and consumer-provided executors.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- Before invoking an executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's JSON Schema and returns a `ToolResponse` describing a rejected property path and constraint without including its value; validation enforces required properties, types, and enums, while an unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects schema violations before execution without disclosing values and preserves unknown-tool errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34))
+- Valid input reaches the executor exactly once and unchanged, including unknown properties and without coercion or defaults; a function-valued definition is resolved and validated against the schema current for each call. ([validated by: passes valid input through unchanged and validates each dynamic definition current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L82))
+- A static schema is compiled once during registration, an invalid static schema throws there with the tool name in the error, and repeated executions do not recompile it. ([validated by: rejects a broken static schema at registration and compiles a valid static schema only there](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L119))
+- A validation rejection is returned through the tool loop as a tool result, allowing the provider to see the reason and retry within the bounded rounds without rejecting `processMessage`. ([validated by: returns a validation rejection to the model so it can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L155))
+
+## Public contract
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` documents this behavior with a one-line comment pointing here: schema rejections are returned as tool responses, while only an unknown tool name throws.
